<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Page
    x:Class="ArtifactX.WinUI3.Views.SettlementPage"
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
    xmlns:ctcontrols="using:CommunityToolkit.WinUI.Controls"
    xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
    xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
    mc:Ignorable="d"
    Background="{ThemeResource ApplicationPageBackgroundThemeBrush}">

    <ScrollViewer>
        <StackPanel Padding="24" Spacing="20">
            <Grid>
                <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="Settlements" FontSize="26" FontWeight="Bold" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                <Button Grid.Column="2" x:Name="PageResetBtn" Content="Reset Settlement Changes" Click="PageResetBtn_Click"
                        Visibility="Collapsed" Style="{StaticResource DangerButtonStyle}" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
            </Grid>

            <TextBlock FontSize="10" Opacity="0.55" TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxWidth="820"
                       Text="FIRST PASS, 2026-07-29 - field names below are inferred by cross-referencing a real settlement's raw save keys against libMBIN's own GcSettlementState class (same field count, same order, plausible values for every match), NOT yet confirmed by editing and reloading in-game the way every Pets field was. Treat everything here as a strong hypothesis to test, not a settled fact - change one field at a time and check in-game what happens."/>

            <StackPanel Spacing="20" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch">
                <TextBlock Text="Owned Settlements" FontSize="14" Opacity="0.8"/>
                <ScrollViewer MaxHeight="104" VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto"
                              HorizontalScrollBarVisibility="Disabled" HorizontalScrollMode="Disabled">
                    <ctcontrols:WrapPanel x:Name="SettlementSelectorPanel" HorizontalSpacing="8" VerticalSpacing="8"/>
                </ScrollViewer>

                <!-- Full width (page's own Padding="24" above is the only margin) rather than
                     the old fixed Width="860" - the Buffs section below can't be given a sane
                     fixed width now that its real length is confirmed unbounded (tested to 19
                     entries with no cap found), so the whole card stretches to use whatever
                     room the window actually has. -->
                <Border BorderBrush="{ThemeResource NmsTextSecondary}" BorderThickness="1"
                        CornerRadius="8" Padding="20" Opacity="0.9" HorizontalAlignment="Stretch">
                    <StackPanel Spacing="18">
                        <StackPanel Spacing="6">
                            <TextBlock Text="Name" FontSize="12" Opacity="0.7"/>
                            <TextBox x:Name="NameEditBox" Width="300" HorizontalAlignment="Left" LostFocus="NameEditBox_LostFocus"/>
                        </StackPanel>

                        <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="32">
                            <StackPanel Spacing="6" Width="160">
                                <TextBlock Text="Owner" FontSize="12" Opacity="0.7"/>
                                <TextBlock x:Name="OwnerTxt" FontSize="14"/>
                            </StackPanel>
                            <StackPanel Spacing="6" Width="160">
                                <TextBlock Text="Culture (Race)" FontSize="12" Opacity="0.7"/>
                                <ComboBox x:Name="RaceBox" Width="150" HorizontalAlignment="Left" SelectionChanged="RaceBox_SelectionChanged"
                                          ToolTipService.ToolTip="Confirmed 2026-07-30 - controls the in-game &quot;X Planetary Settlement&quot; subtitle, but the game translates it to a real species name: Traders-&gt;Gek, Warriors-&gt;Vy'keen, Explorers-&gt;Korvax (confirmed by testing each). The other 6 options are untested. Confirmed this does NOT affect the separate &quot;Dominant Lifeform&quot; stat on the deeper settlement stats screen - that's cosmetic-only, not tied to this field."/>
                            </StackPanel>
                            <StackPanel Spacing="6" Width="160">
                                <TextBlock Text="Population" FontSize="12" Opacity="0.7"/>
                                <NumberBox x:Name="PopulationBox" Width="140" HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                                           Minimum="0" SpinButtonPlacementMode="Hidden"
                                           ValueChanged="PopulationBox_ValueChanged" LostFocus="PopulationBox_LostFocus"/>
                            </StackPanel>
                        </StackPanel>

                        <StackPanel Spacing="8">
                            <TextBlock Text="Stats" FontSize="14" FontWeight="SemiBold"/>
                            <TextBlock FontSize="10" Opacity="0.55" TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxWidth="700"
                                       Text="Matches libMBIN's SettlementStatTypeEnum (8 members) positionally - real sampled values varied widely in scale, so no min/max is enforced here. Confirmed 2026-07-29: Debt and Happiness track the in-game display closely. Max Population and Production DO feed the in-game Max Population/Productivity numbers - confirmed by setting Production to 2,000,000,000 and seeing an in-game Productivity of ~2,000,301,113 - but ADDITIVELY, combined with a baseline from Buildings/Perks, not as a direct overwrite (e.g. Max Population 0-&gt;100 moved the shown max from ~55 to 159, not to exactly 100). Upkeep/Sentinels are assumed to work the same way but haven't been pushed to a distinctive test value yet to fully confirm. OBSERVED 2026-07-30: setting Bug Attack to 1000 was followed by a real in-game &quot;biological infestation&quot; event at that same settlement (a Vile Queen boss fight to purge) - suggestive it drives that event, though not yet isolated from settlements occasionally getting infestations on their own."/>
                            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="24">
                                <StackPanel Spacing="6" Width="120">
                                    <TextBlock Text="Max Population" Opacity="0.7" FontSize="11"/>
                                    <NumberBox x:Name="Stat0Box" Width="110" HorizontalAlignment="Left" SpinButtonPlacementMode="Hidden" ValueChanged="Stat0Box_ValueChanged"/>
                                </StackPanel>
                                <StackPanel Spacing="6" Width="120">
                                    <TextBlock Text="Happiness" Opacity="0.7" FontSize="11"/>
                                    <NumberBox x:Name="Stat1Box" Width="110" HorizontalAlignment="Left" SpinButtonPlacementMode="Hidden" ValueChanged="Stat1Box_ValueChanged"/>
                                </StackPanel>
                                <StackPanel Spacing="6" Width="120">
                                    <TextBlock Text="Production" Opacity="0.7" FontSize="11"/>
                                    <NumberBox x:Name="Stat2Box" Width="110" HorizontalAlignment="Left" SpinButtonPlacementMode="Hidden" ValueChanged="Stat2Box_ValueChanged"/>
                                </StackPanel>
                                <StackPanel Spacing="6" Width="120">
                                    <TextBlock Text="Upkeep" Opacity="0.7" FontSize="11"/>
                                    <NumberBox x:Name="Stat3Box" Width="110" HorizontalAlignment="Left" SpinButtonPlacementMode="Hidden" ValueChanged="Stat3Box_ValueChanged"/>
                                </StackPanel>
                            </StackPanel>
                            <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="24">
                                <StackPanel Spacing="6" Width="120">
                                    <TextBlock Text="Sentinels" Opacity="0.7" FontSize="11"/>
                                    <NumberBox x:Name="Stat4Box" Width="110" HorizontalAlignment="Left" SpinButtonPlacementMode="Hidden" ValueChanged="Stat4Box_ValueChanged"/>
                                </StackPanel>
                                <StackPanel Spacing="6" Width="120">
                                    <TextBlock Text="Debt" Opacity="0.7" FontSize="11"/>
                                    <NumberBox x:Name="Stat5Box" Width="110" HorizontalAlignment="Left" SpinButtonPlacementMode="Hidden" ValueChanged="Stat5Box_ValueChanged"/>
                                </StackPanel>
                                <StackPanel Spacing="6" Width="120">
                                    <TextBlock Text="Alert" Opacity="0.7" FontSize="11"/>
                                    <NumberBox x:Name="Stat6Box" Width="110" HorizontalAlignment="Left" SpinButtonPlacementMode="Hidden" ValueChanged="Stat6Box_ValueChanged"/>
                                </StackPanel>
                                <StackPanel Spacing="6" Width="120">
                                    <TextBlock Text="Bug Attack" Opacity="0.7" FontSize="11"/>
                                    <NumberBox x:Name="Stat7Box" Width="110" HorizontalAlignment="Left" SpinButtonPlacementMode="Hidden" ValueChanged="Stat7Box_ValueChanged"/>
                                </StackPanel>
                            </StackPanel>
                        </StackPanel>

                        <StackPanel Spacing="8">
                            <Grid>
                                <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                    <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                                    <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                                </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                                <TextBlock Grid.Column="0" Text="Buffs (Settlement Features)" FontSize="14" FontWeight="SemiBold" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                                <StackPanel Grid.Column="1" Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8">
                                    <Button x:Name="AddPerkSlotBtn" Content="Add Buff Slot" Click="AddPerkSlotBtn_Click"/>
                                    <Button x:Name="FillEmptyPerksBtn" Content="Fill Empty Slots" Click="FillEmptyPerksBtn_Click"/>
                                </StackPanel>
                            </Grid>
                            <TextBlock FontSize="10" Opacity="0.55" TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxWidth="700"
                                       Text="Confirmed 2026-07-29 - real names/descriptions resolved directly from the game's own settlement perks table (matched exactly against a real settlement's in-game &quot;Settlement Features&quot; panel, e.g. &quot;Public artworks - Improves citizen happiness&quot;). Each row is one Perks array entry; &quot;(None)&quot; means that entry is empty. Picking a different perk swaps just that entry's id, dropping any per-instance roll suffix some perks carry (e.g. &quot;PROC_FUN#09286&quot;). A perk labeled &quot;Proc&quot; shows raw text like &quot;%FUN_ADJ% %FUN_FACILITY%&quot; here only - CONFIRMED 2026-07-30 the game generates real, readable, themed flavor text for these on its own even with no roll suffix supplied - safe to pick freely, no suffix needed. CORRECTED 2026-07-30: this array is NOT capped at 8 - that was a real analysis mistake (the game field is an unbounded list, not a fixed array), proven wrong when a real settlement grew to 10 features through normal play alone. CONFIRMED 2026-07-30: grown to 19 entries via &quot;Add Buff Slot&quot; and tested in-game - all 19 loaded fine across 4 paginated panel pages, no crash, no cap found. Treat this as effectively unbounded. &quot;Fill Empty Slots&quot; randomly picks a real perk for every currently-empty entry, leaving anything you've already set untouched."/>
                            <!-- Perks are grouped into cards of 6 (built in code-behind, see
                                 BuildPerksPanel) rather than one long flat list, since the
                                 array's real length is confirmed unbounded. A WrapPanel flows
                                 cards left-to-right and drops extras to new rows automatically
                                 as the window narrows - no fixed page-width assumption needed. -->
                            <ctcontrols:WrapPanel x:Name="PerksPanel" HorizontalSpacing="16" VerticalSpacing="16"/>
                        </StackPanel>
                    </StackPanel>
                </Border>
            </StackPanel>
        </StackPanel>
    </ScrollViewer>
</Page>
